  <div class="body-container body-container--blog-post body-container--custom-post-template body-container--job-post">

    
    <div class="content-wrapper container">
        <article class="blog-post">
            <h1 class="job-post-title"><span id="hs_cos_wrapper_name" class="hs_cos_wrapper hs_cos_wrapper_meta_field hs_cos_wrapper_type_text" style="" data-hs-cos-general-type="meta_field" data-hs-cos-type="text">Project Success Manager</span></h1>
            <div class="blog-post__body">

                <span id="hs_cos_wrapper_post_body" class="hs_cos_wrapper hs_cos_wrapper_meta_field hs_cos_wrapper_type_rich_text" style="" data-hs-cos-general-type="meta_field" data-hs-cos-type="rich_text"><h4 style="border: none; font-size: 24px;"><span style="color: #333333;"><span style="color: #308bf5; background-color: #ffffff;">Reports to:</span></span></h4>
<!--more-->
<p style="border: none;"><span style="color: #333333;">The Project Success Manager will report directly to Free Range’s Managing Director, is accountable to clients and manages cross functional teams. </span><span style="color: #308bf5; background-color: #ffffff;"></span></p>
<h4 style="border: none; font-size: 24px;"><span style="color: #308bf5; background-color: #ffffff;">Job Overview:</span></h4>
<p style="border: none;"><span style="color: #333333;">In this role you will be responsible for communicating with clients and cross-functional teams to manage 3-7 projects (depending on project sizes) with concurrent workstreams. You will work with clients throughout project life cycles to plan resourcing that informs roadmaps, timelines, and recommendations, providing Free Range customers with a positive and consultative experience. You are a team leader who effectively harnesses the talents of others. You contribute to the creative process while efficiently moving toward final deliverables.</span></p>
<h4 style="border: none; font-size: 24px;"><span style="color: #308bf5; background-color: #ffffff;">Responsibilities and Duties:</span></h4>
<p style="border: none;"><span style="color: #333333;">Specifically, you will be responsible for the following duties and tasks:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 2pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Client Management.</span>
<ul>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 2pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Weekly meetings for presentations and feedback as needed</span></li>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 2pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Gantt Charts and other reporting</span></li>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 2pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Notes and Progress tracking</span></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 2pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Project Management</span>
<ul>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 2pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Recommendations</span></li>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 2pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Approvals &amp; Requirements</span></li>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 2pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">SCRUM/Kanban management</span></li>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 2pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Content Entry and Occasional Writing</span></li>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 2pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">P&amp;L and Other Reporting</span></li>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 2pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Testing &amp; Quality Assurance</span></li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 style="border: none; font-size: 24px;"><span style="color: #333333;"><span style="color: #308bf5; background-color: #ffffff;">Qualifications:</span></span></h4>
<p style="border: none;"><span style="color: #333333;">Below are the minimum qualifications necessary for someone to fill this position.</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 4.8pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Bachelor, MBA preferred, or other Equivalent Educational Experiences</span></li>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 4.8pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">2-10 years project/product management experience </span></li>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 4.8pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Likes working with fast paced teams</span></li>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 4.8pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Firm understanding of different business models </span></li>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 4.8pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Understand Design Systems and UX/UI Concepts</span></li>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 4.8pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Experience working with Nonprofits is a plus</span></li>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 4.8pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Technical Experience is a plus</span></li>
<li style="border: none; margin-top: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 4.8pt;"><span style="font-size: 10px; color: #333333;"> </span><span style="color: #333333;">Marketing Experience is a plus</span></li>
</ul>
<h4 style="border: none; font-size: 24px;"><span style="color: #333333;"><span style="color: #308bf5; background-color: #ffffff;">Compensation:</span></span></h4>
<p style="border: none;"><span style="color: #333333;">For the right fit, this will turn into a full-time position with Salary + Benefits + PTO ($60K-$80K /year based on location and level of experience). Initially we are hiring hourly ($30 - $45 /hour based on location and experience)</span><span style="color: #333333;"><span style="color: #308bf5; background-color: #ffffff;"></span></span></p>
<h4 style="border: none; font-size: 24px;"><span style="color: #333333;"><span style="color: #308bf5; background-color: #ffffff;">About Free Range:</span></span></h4>
<p style="border: none;"><span style="color: #333333;">Free Range Studios, LLC is a small, growing creative group of consultants, writers, designers, animators, producers, and developers. It’s our proven process and our suite of services that make us an easy choice for our partners and clients. We all bring unique skills, experience, and perspectives. We work as a team to build memorable brands and kick-ass products, and we have fun doing it.</span></p></span>

                

